==========================================================================================================================
PART E -- CANDIDATE B: a second scalar with a stable condensate, DECOUPLED FROM THE CLOCK.
          The tachyon came from the clock's coupling to the condensate; is the decoupled version safe?
==========================================================================================================================
  Derived symbolically here rather than asserted.  Perturb the clock, tau = t + T, on a flat FRW
  background with scale factor a.  Then
      X = -g^{ab} d_a tau d_b tau,   n_mu = -d_mu tau / sqrt(X),   Q = n^mu d_mu phi,
  and the point is that Q -- and therefore ANY function K(Q) -- depends on T.  Expand to second order in
  the perturbations (T, dphi) and read off the coefficient of the T-gradient squared.
  
      Q to second order:    Q = Qbar + Qbar*epsilon**2*vT**2/(2*a**2) + epsilon*up - epsilon**2*vT*vp/a**2
      the quadratic action from K(Q) = K_2 Q^2 contains:
          coefficient of (dT/dx)^2      :  K2*Qbar**2/a**2      <-- THE CLOCK MASS TERM
          coefficient of (dT/dx)(dphi/dx):  -2*K2*Qbar/a**2
          coefficient of (dphi/dt)^2    :  K2
  
      So the clock's induced gradient-mass coefficient is EXACTLY K_2 Qbar^2 / a^2: proportional to the
      square of the CONDENSATE BACKGROUND, and vanishing identically when that background is zero.  With
      K_2 = -|K_2| the sign is tachyonic, and the clock's own kinetic operator carries the same k^2, which
      is why the rate is k-independent -- reproducing rate^2 = |K_2| Qbar^2 (...) / c_14 of g03w.
      THIS DERIVES, rather than asserts, why setting Q_0 = 0 cures the tachyon.
  [PASS] P1 the clock tachyon's coefficient is exactly proportional to the condensate background Qbar^2, so it is the CLOCK'S COUPLING to the condensate -- not the condensate's energy density -- that creates it   (coefficient of (dT/dx)^2 = K2*Qbar**2/a**2, which is K_2 Qbar^2/a^2 exactly and vanishes identically at Qbar = 0.  This reproduces THE_COMPLETE_THEORY 3.2's cure (Q_0 = 0) from the algebra rather than from its conclusion)

  NOW THE LANE'S QUESTION.  Give the new component a kinetic function that is a mixture: a fraction lambda
  built from the clock-projected derivative Q_chi = n^mu d_mu chi, and (1 - lambda) built from the fully
  covariant X_chi = -g^{ab} d_a chi d_b chi.  lambda = 1 is the original condensate; lambda = 0 is a field
  whose action does not contain the clock's normal at all.
      coefficient of (dT/dx)^2 in the MIXED kinetic function: K2*Qbar**2*lambda/a**2
      the covariant piece X_chi = (Qbar + epsilon*up)**2 - epsilon**2*vp**2/a**2 contains no T at all: dX_chi/d(dT/dt) = 0, dX_chi/d(dT/dx) = 0
  [PASS] P2 a component DECOUPLED FROM THE CLOCK (lambda = 0, i.e. a covariant kinetic term with no n) evades the tachyon by construction -- the mechanism that killed the original condensate does not act on it   (the clock mass coefficient is lambda K_2 Qbar^2/a^2, exactly zero at lambda = 0, and the covariant kinetic scalar is identically independent of the clock. So YES: the specific mechanism that killed the original condensate is evaded, and it is evaded structurally rather than by tuning)
      at the exhibited point c_14 = 1e-6: rate <= H at every a needs lambda Omega_chi <= Omega_m c_14/3, i.e. lambda <= 3.947e-07
      at the PPN ceiling c_14 = 2.5e-5: rate <= H at every a needs lambda Omega_chi <= Omega_m c_14/3, i.e. lambda <= 9.868e-06
  [FAIL] P3 an APPROXIMATE decoupling is enough -- a component that is mostly, but not exactly, decoupled from the clock is still safe   (it is not: the clock-coupled fraction must satisfy lambda <= 3.95e-07 at the exhibited point and <= 9.87e-06 even at the loosest PPN-allowed c_14. The decoupling must therefore be EXACT to parts in 1e6-1e7, i.e. enforced by a symmetry, not merely small. Any operator that mixes the new field with the clock at loop level or through the metric at O(1) reopens the tachyon)
  
  P4.  A stable scalar condensate with V = m^2 chi^2/2 oscillating with m >> H behaves as pressureless dust; the only thing that distinguishes it from cold matter is its de Broglie scale.
       confining it inside the cluster core (sigma = 886 km/s, r <~ 200 kpc, which R3/L41 D3 require) needs m >= 1.08e-26 eV;
       confining it inside a classical dwarf (sigma = 10 km/s, r ~ 1 kpc) needs m >= 1.92e-22 eV.
       Above ~1e-21 eV the soliton core is sub-parsec and every observable in the specification is identical to that of cold collisionless matter.
  [FAIL] P4 the clock-decoupled condensate is OBSERVATIONALLY DISTINCT from candidate A, i.e. it is a different addition rather than the same one in different clothing   (it is not: the specification's own requirements force m >= 1.9e-22 eV (dwarf) and m >= 1.1e-26 eV (cluster core), and above that mass the component is pressureless, collisionless, has no phase-space floor and carries an NFW-like profile -- i.e. it IS candidate A. It also fails N1 for exactly the same reason, because N1 is about the kernel double-counting the added mass and does not care what the mass is made of. Candidate B is therefore a REALISATION of candidate A, not a cheaper alternative, and it costs one extra parameter (m) and one exactness assumption (P3))

==========================================================================================================================
PART F -- CANDIDATE C: a component sourced by the MOND scalar rather than by the clock.
==========================================================================================================================
  The MOND sector is J(Y + xi^2 |grad_perp V|^2) with Y = q^{ab} d_a phi d_b phi, i.e. a function of the
  SPATIAL gradient of phi on the clock's leaves.  Two readings, both tested.
  
    (i) the HOMOGENEOUS piece.  On an FRW slice every spatial gradient vanishes, so Y = 0 identically and
        the sector contributes rho = J(0), p = -J(0): an exact w = -1.  L32/L40's zero-mode theorem is the
        same statement at the level of the action -- J -> J + C is exactly degenerate with Lambda.  A
        component that is exactly a cosmological constant cannot cluster and cannot be the cold component.
  [FAIL] Q1 the MOND sector's homogeneous piece can supply a clustering cold component   (it cannot: Y = 0 on a homogeneous slice, so the sector's equation of state is exactly w = -1.0 and its density is a_-independent. Its perturbation is second order in gradients (Y = |grad dphi|^2), so it cannot source the background either. This is the zero-mode theorem of L32/H-C read as a cosmology rather than as a statement about kappa)
  
    (ii) the GRADIENT piece.  This is not a new candidate at all -- it is the framework's EXISTING phantom,
        already measured: short by 1.49-1.99x at R500 in lensing and dynamics alike, with a projected
        shear log-slope of -0.309 against the measured -0.851 (X4), and exceeding the kernel's
        own bounded-boost ceiling by 5.2x at 40 kpc in cluster cores.
  [FAIL] Q2 the MOND sector's gradient piece supplies the cluster amount and shape   (it does not, and this is the deposited theory's own measured failure rather than a new result: shear log-slope -0.309 against -0.851, a difference of +0.542 +/- 0.060 = 9 sigma, because a matter-sourced scalar's phantom is a near-uniform sheet. A species whose MASS depends on phi is a different proposal, but it still has to carry the mass itself -- the coupling redistributes the source, it does not create it -- so it is candidate A plus a coupling, i.e. strictly more than the minimum)

==========================================================================================================================
PART G -- CANDIDATE D: structures the recorded no-go never tested, because they are neither a particle
          nor a condensate.
==========================================================================================================================
    (i) MACROSCOPIC DARK OBJECTS (primordial black holes, or any compact relic).  The recorded no-go
        closes Pauli-limited fermions, wave dark matter, four condensate constructions and the thermal
        relic -- every one of which is a bound on a LIGHT species' phase-space density or free-streaming.
        A macroscopic object has neither: at M = 1e-12 Msun its de Broglie wavelength is 5.98e-59 m and the Tremaine-Gunn floor is inapplicable by ~60 orders of magnitude.
  [FAIL] T1 a macroscopic dark component (PBH-like) satisfies the specification AND is a genuinely different addition from candidate A   (it satisfies the specification -- it is cold, collisionless, has no phase-space floor, carries an NFW profile and the same abundance -- but on every requirement R1-R11 it is INDISTINGUISHABLE from candidate A, and it fails N1 identically. It is a realisation of the minimum addition, not an alternative to it, and it inherits its own mass-window constraints (microlensing, CMB accretion) which this lane does not evaluate)
  
    (ii) UNDETECTED BARYONS.  L41's B5 left this door OPEN at pair scale (5.0x the K-band mass spread
        inside 132 kpc puts only 0.0017 M_b inside 10 kpc, well within the galaxy gate).  It is closed at
        CLUSTER scale, and closed by the clusters' own measured baryon fraction rather than by BBN:
        making the cluster residual baryonic drives f_bar from 0.149 to 1.000, i.e. clusters would be 100% baryons against the cosmic 0.156.
  [FAIL] T2 undetected baryons can supply the cluster amount   (they cannot: f_bar would have to be 1.00 against the cosmic 0.156, a factor 6.4. The pair-scale door L41 left open therefore cannot be the SAME mechanism as the cluster source, so taking it would require TWO additions rather than one -- which is not a minimum addition. (Whether the circumgalactic budget allows it at pair scale remains, as L41 said, a literature question this repository does not settle))

==========================================================================================================================
PART H -- THE COST AGAINST THE ELEVEN GATES THE DEPOSITED THEORY PASSES.
==========================================================================================================================
  [PASS] N4 [gate H11, the one that killed the original condensate] adding a cold component minimally coupled to g leaves the clock-tachyon gate satisfied   (it does: by P1 the clock's induced mass term is lambda K_2 Qbar^2/a^2, and a component in the matter sector (or any component with lambda = 0) contributes exactly zero to it. The gate stays satisfied IDENTICALLY, as it is with Q_0 = 0 -- adding mass to S_m does not reintroduce the instability that deleting the condensate cured. This is the single most important cost that is NOT paid)
  [PASS] N5 [mode count and health] adding a cold component leaves the gravitational sector's mode count and health unchanged   (it does: the gravitational sector remains 2 tensor + 1 clock + 1 MOND scalar = 4 healthy modes, and the 'N_grav = 2' requirement was already recorded as FAIL read as a total. A cold component adds at most one matter degree of freedom (zero, for a fluid or a macroscopic relic), which is not a gravitational mode and does not touch A_0 = 0.4615 > 0, the hyperbolicity at sigma*, or the scalar's Bogoliubov dispersion)
  N6 Solar System.  A smooth cold halo of the locally measured density puts
      M_DM(< Saturn) = 0.0104 Msun/pc^3 x (4pi/3)(9.583 AU)^3 = 4.37e-15 Msun against Pitjev-Pitjeva's 6.7e-11 Msun -- 15338x below the bound.
  [PASS] N6 [Solar-System bounds] adding a cold component leaves the Saturn phantom-mass bound intact   (4.37e-15 Msun against the 6.7e-11 Msun bound, a margin of 15338x. The Cassini quadrupole, the sunward-acceleration bound and the coherence length xi are untouched because a cold component adds no new field gradient)
  [PASS] N7 [preferred-frame parameters] adding a cold component leaves alpha_1, alpha_2, alpha_3 and gamma unchanged   (it does: alpha_1 = -4 c_14 = -4.00e-06 and alpha_2 = (c_14/2)(1/sigma - 1) = -2.02e-07 are functions of (c_14, c_2, sigma) alone, and a component minimally coupled to g enters PPN only as source mass. The one thing it DOES change is the preferred-frame velocity budget: the cold component shares the matter frame, so no new alpha_1 v^2 term appears)
  [PASS] N8 [BBN] adding a cold component leaves the BBN gate intact   (it does: a cold component contributes Delta N_eff = 0 and does not move K_B <= 0.25 or G_cos/G_N - 1 = -2.5e-6. It DOES set Omega_m = 0.315, which is an input the deposited theory previously had no way to supply at all)
  [PASS] N9 [CMB and linear growth] adding a cold component repairs the two gates the deposited theory fails outright, at no cost in the growth sector   (it does, and this is the payoff: on the closure locus c_2|K_2| = (2 - K_B)^2 the linear MOND source is S_eff = 0.0e+00 EXACTLY, so the linear growth equation with a cold component is ALGEBRAICALLY IDENTICAL to LambdaCDM's. The third acoustic peak, sigma_8, S_8 and P(k) follow. Nothing here is a prediction: it is LambdaCDM's cosmology imported wholesale, and it should be stated as that)
  
  N3 the bounded boost.  The action predicts g_obs - g_N <= C a_0 = 6.06e-11 / 7.30e-11 m/s^2 with no free parameter, and THE_COMPLETE_THEORY calls it the falsifier that LambdaCDM structurally cannot make. It is a statement about g_N, and it is TESTABLE only while g_N = g_bar.
      with an abundance-matched cold component present, 36% of SPARC points have g_halo alone ABOVE C a_0, so the observed g_obs - g_bar is dominated by the halo and carries no information about the ceiling.
  [FAIL] N3 the bounded-boost ceiling remains a testable prediction once a cold component is present   (it does not: the ceiling survives as a statement about g_N, but g_N is no longer observable -- 36% (canonical) / 30% (alt) of SPARC points have the halo term alone above C a_0. The programme's sharpest falsifier is converted from a prediction into a statement about an unobservable, and that is a real loss that must be stated as one)

==========================================================================================================================
PART I -- THE SHARP QUESTION: with a cold component present, is the MOND sector still doing work?
==========================================================================================================================
  W1 the tightness claim, reproduced and then corrected as L28 corrects it:
      kernel at frozen a_0, ZERO parameters per galaxy : 0.145 dex  [L16/L28: 0.142]
      abundance-matched NFW, ZERO parameters per galaxy: 0.171 dex  [L16/L28: 0.171]
      NFW with M200 and c FREE, TWO parameters/galaxy  : 0.061 dex  [L28's prior-shrunk 0.085]
  [FAIL] W1 the kernel's tightness is a discriminant against a cold component -- i.e. the halo cannot reach the kernel's scatter even when allowed its own freedom   (it is not, and L28 already said so: a per-galaxy NFW reaches 0.061 dex against the kernel's 0.145. What survives is a PARSIMONY claim -- the kernel achieves 0.145 dex with ZERO parameters per galaxy where the halo needs two -- and it must never be written as a discriminant against LambdaCDM)
  [PASS] W2 the parsimony claim survives the addition   (it does, and it is the one thing that does: at zero parameters per galaxy on both sides the kernel gives 0.145 dex against the abundance-matched halo's 0.171 (ratio 1.18x). But note what it is a claim ABOUT: it is a statement that the RAR is tight, not that the kernel causes it, and N1 shows the kernel cannot be present at the same time as the mass that would explain the rest)
  
  W3 a_0(z).  THE_COMPLETE_THEORY's surviving distinctive prediction is that the deep-MOND baryonic Tully-Fisher zero point is flat to <1% to z = 5 against LambdaCDM's +0.33 dex by z = 2.5. That is a prediction about a regime in which the KERNEL sets the dynamics. With a cold component at f = 1 the high-z rotators are halo-dominated (N1/N3), so the deep-MOND zero point is not the theory's prediction any more; it becomes LambdaCDM's, plus a bounded kernel correction of at most C a_0.
  [FAIL] W4 the a_0(z) prediction survives the addition as a discriminant   (it does not survive as a CLEAN one. The prediction is a statement about a system whose dynamics the kernel sets; with a cold component the same rotator is halo-dominated and the BTFR zero point is set by the halo, with the kernel adding at most C a_0 = 6.1e-11 m/s^2 on top. The measurement (a deep-MOND lensed rotator at z ~ 2-2.5 to +-0.13 dex) remains worth making -- it discriminates the NO-addition theory from LambdaCDM -- but it stops being a test of the theory once the addition is made)
  [FAIL] W5 [THE SHARP QUESTION] with a cold collisionless component present at the abundance the CMB fixes, the MOND sector is still doing identifiable work in galaxy dynamics   (it is not, and the reason is specific rather than generic. At f = 1 the kernel plus the halo overshoots the measured rotation curves by 1.82x in acceleration (N1), and the galaxy ceiling f <= 0.355 is 2.8x below the CMB's f = 1 (64 sigma, N2). The one place the MOND sector DOES still do work is the partial-cold cosmology N2a exhibits, f ~ 0.29, where the kernel supplies the rest at both galaxy and cluster scale -- but that cosmology has a third of the observed cold-matter density and is excluded by the CMB. So, listed in full and without padding, what the MOND sector still supplies once the addition is made at f = 1: (i) the a_0-Lambda TIE, a_0 = kappa c sqrt(G rho_Lambda), with kappa = 0.4998/0.6023 FITTED -- a numerological relation, not a derivation, by L32's zero-mode theorem; (ii) a PARSIMONY claim, 0.145 / 0.142 dex at zero parameters per galaxy against the halo's 0.171, which W1 shows is NOT a discriminant because a per-galaxy halo reaches 0.061; (iii) a BOUNDED-BOOST ceiling that N3 shows is no longer testable; and (iv) the fact that WITHOUT the addition it is a complete, Solar-System-safe, galaxy-correct relativistic theory. That is the whole list, and (i)-(iii) are the parsimony claim, the tie and a ceiling -- not dynamical work)

