PART J -- VERDICT
==========================================================================================================================
  [PASS] V1 [VERDICT] a MINIMUM ADDITION exists: some single component supplies everything the deposited theory is missing above a galaxy   (it does, and it is a COLD COLLISIONLESS COMPONENT IN THE MATTER SECTOR, minimally coupled to g and decoupled from the clock. It satisfies R1 (0.4 sigma), R3 (-1.56 vs -1.44), R4 (-0.851 vs -0.851), R5, R6 (31.0 vs 30.9), R8, R9, R10, R12 and R13; it leaves the clock tachyon satisfied identically (N4), the mode count and health untouched (N5), the Solar System untouched (N6), the preferred-frame parameters untouched (N7) and BBN untouched (N8); and it repairs the CMB and linear growth exactly (N9). Candidates B, C and D are either realisations of it or already closed)
  [FAIL] V2 the minimum addition is FREE -- it can be made without breaking any gate the deposited theory currently passes   (it cannot. It breaks the galaxy-scale non-overshoot gate outright (N1: median RAR residual -0.259 dex at f = 1, an overshoot of 1.82x in acceleration), because the action's MOND scalar is sourced by the TOTAL potential and therefore amplifies the very mass that was added to replace it. The three admissible cold fractions have an EMPTY intersection: galaxies <= 0.355, clusters 0.32 +/- 0.10, CMB 1.00 +/- 0.01 -- and the binding constraint is the CMB, a factor 2.8 away, not the clusters, which N2a shows can actually be reconciled with galaxies at f ~ 0.3. It also voids the bounded-boost falsifier (N3), blunts a_0(z) (W4), and costs the stellar-to-halo-mass relation as a new free function of host mass (M5))

